      "url": "https://www.custify.com/contact"
    },
    "description": "This is the documentation for APIs from the Custify App.\n# INTRODUCTION\nThe Custify API is a RESTful API. The requests and responses are formatted according to the JSON API specification.\n\nIt might happen that you requested to run your Custify application within a data center that's optimized for your location. In this case, you might have to use a different API endpoint URL, instead of https://api.custify.com, to optimize your calls. You'll find your API URL within the app at [Settings -> Developers -> API Key](https://app.custify.com/settings/developer/api-key).\n### Data imports\nIn general, there are 3 ways to synchronize your customer data and their events with Custify *on an ongoing basis*:\n- The Custify API\n- The Custify JavaScript snippet\n- An available integration with one of your systems (e.g., via Segment.com)\n\nThis documentation covers the Custify API and JavaScript snippet. Individual integrations are documented separately.\n\nFor the *initial* data import, you have several options:\n- Write a script that uses the Custify API to run through your customers and call the API for each one of them\n- An available integration into one of your systems that pulls the customer data from there (e.g., Hubspot)\n\n### Data types\nThe data type of the first submission (import or API request) defines the data type of an attribute or event metadata within Custify (Boolean, Integer, Date, or String). We'll try to auto-detect the type of the attribute (or event metadata) in the following order: Date, Number and Boolean.\nIf none of these types will match the type of the attribute will be set to String.\n\nFor an attribute or event metadata to be detected as Date it should be sent in the following ISO 8601 formats: `YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm:ss`, `YYYY-MM-DD`, `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss`, `YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm`, `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss.SSS`, `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ssZ`, `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss.SSSZ` or `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss.SSSSSSZ`.\nOtherwise, they'll be treated as Strings. These attributes must be sent as UTC dates or using the timezone format. Example:\n```json\n{\n    \"company_id\": \"25\",\n    \"custom_attributes\": {\n        \"date\": \"2020-09-25T10:00:00\",\n        \"date_format\": \"2020-09-25T10:00:00.000\"\n    }\n}\n```\n\nFor an attribute (or event metadata) to be detected as a Number you could send it as in the following example:\n```json\n{\n    \"company_id\": \"25\",\n    \"custom_attributes\": {\n        \"team_mates\": 5,\n        \"team_mates_number\": \"7\",\n        \"also_number\": 10.2,\n        \"other_number\": \"5.4\"\n    }\n}\n```\n\nFor an attribute (or event metadata) to be detected as a Boolean you could send it as in the following example:\n```json\n{\n    \"company_id\": \"25\",\n    \"custom_attributes\": {\n        \"unsubscribed\": true,\n        \"unsubscribed_false\": \"FALSE\"\n        \"unsubscribed_true\": \"true\"\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThis initial data type is later used to compare attributes of different entities (e.g., when creating segments or searching). Although you can send a different data type later on, the first submission defines the data type that Custify uses for this field. We highly recommend never switching the data type for your custom attributes. If you need to change it, submit a new attribute for all customers with the new data type.\n\nYou can also set values to null. You might do this, for example, if you no longer have a valid value for one of your attributes.\n\n### Rate limiting\nThe API may limit the submission of requests for your application. The limits are managed as an allowed number of operations per time window; an operation might be a read or an update. If you're not on a special enterprise plan, API calls are limited to `100 requests` per `10 seconds` time window. If the limit is reached, a `429 Too Many Requests` response code will be returned along with the following headers:\n\n#### Rate limit headers:\n- `X-RateLimit-Limit`: Maximum number of operations allowed in the current window\n- `X-RateLimit-Remaining`: Number of operations left in the current window.\n- `Retry-After`: Number of seconds starting from the first request in the window after the rate limit window will be reset.\n\nFurther limitations on certain objects (like the maximum length of strings, range of integers) are documented in the individual API calls.\n\n### Postman collection\nPostman is a tool that lets you build and test HTTP requests in an easy-to-use interface without configuring a full development environment. The Custify Postman Collection is a set of preconfigured requests that make it possible to get started with the Custify API from Postman without having to manually configure the requests.\nYou can download the collection from here => (<a href=\"postman_collection.json\" download>POSTMAN collection</a>). To use the collection you can create a new environment (let's say `Custify`) and create the 2 needed variables `ApiUrl` and `ApiKey` which are available here [Settings -> Developers -> API Key](https://app.custify.com/settings/developer/api-key).\n\n# AUTHENTICATION\n### API\nWhen you sign up for an account, you're given your account ID. This ID is visible within [Settings -> Developers -> API Key](https://app.custify.com/settings/developer/api-key). *Never share the API key and only use the API key for API calls, not for JavaScript calls*. Keep it guarded and secure, *as anyone with this key will have full read and write access to your data*.\n\nYou authenticate to the Custify API by providing your API key in the request header (`Authorization: Bearer <API_KEY>`).\n<security-definitions />\n### JavaScript snippet\nWhen you sign up for an account, you're given your account ID. This ID will be visible to you within the Settings -> Developer section.\n# JAVASCRIPT\nWe offer an easy and fast integration via a JavaScript snippet, a block of code you can insert in pages of your app. It's a fast way to send data to the Custify app and the ideal way to track events like clicked buttons or menu items and/or to track time spent in your product.\n## Send data using the JavaScript snippet\nThe JavaScript snippet is a low-impact way to send data to [api.custify.com](https://api.custify.com). While an API integration is more flexible, this is a quick way to get started.\n\n### How to use the JavaScript snippet to send data\n\n#### Step 1: Add the basic JavaScript\nOn every page that you want to track events (e.g., button clicks) or to track the time spent in the product, include the script found at [Settings -> Developers -> JS snippet](https://app.custify.com/settings/developer/js-snippet) just before the closing </body> tag.\n\n#### Step 2: Identify your account and the user\nEvery event within your application  (e.g., \u201cbutton clicked\u201d or \u201clogin\u201d) or the time spent in product is generated from a specific user. For Custify to know which of the users it should attribute the event(s) to, you need to specify the user with an ID and/or email address before sending an event.\nIf the user is part of one or more companies you can link the event to a specific company using the attribute company_id. This attribute is optional.\n- The user ID is referenced in the code below as `USER_ID` and represents the unique ID of the user *within your systems/CRMs*. It's part of the API call to create that user in the first place.\n- The email is referenced as `USER_EMAIL` and represents the unique email of the user within your systems/CRMs.\n- The company is referenced as `COMPANY_ID` and represents the unique ID of the company within your systems/CRMs.\n\nFor the identification of the account and user, you need to add the identification function to your code *beneath the aforementioned basic Javascript*:\n```javascript\n<script type=\"text/javascript\">\n    _ctrack.identify({\n        userId: 'USER_ID', // Your Id of the user\n        email: 'USER_EMAIL', // Email of the user\n        company_id: 'COMPANY_ID' // Your Id of the company\n    });\n</script>\n```\nCustify recommends that you use both userID and email to ensure that users can be identified correctly. The user must already exist in your Custify application before you send events through the JavaScript snippet.\n\n#### Step 3: Track events\nSimple page view tracking can be done by the following snippet:\n```javascript\n<script type=\"text/javascript\">\n    _ctrack.track(\"EVENT_NAME\", {\n      \"METADATA1\": \"VALUE1\",\n      \"METADATA2\": \"VALUE2\",\n      ...\n    });\n</script>\n```\nEvent tracking (i.e., after a button click) can be done using the following snippets as examples:\n\n*pure Javascript*\n\n```html\n<button onclick='_ctrack.track(\"EVENT_NAME\", {\"METADATA1\": \"VALUE1\", \"METADATA2\": \"VALUE2\", ...});'>Button</button>\n```\n\n*using jQuery*\n```javascript\n<script src=\"jquery-3.3.1.min.js\"></script>\n<script type=\"text/javascript\">\n  $(document).ready(function () {\n      $('#button').click(function () {\n          _ctrack.track(\"EVENT_NAME\", {\n            \"METADATA1\": \"VALUE1\",\n            \"METADATA2\": \"VALUE2\",\n            ...\n          });\n      });\n  });\n</script>\n```\n*The second parameter of the `track` function should be a JSON object carrying the additional metadata for that specific event*.\n\nOne possible example for a tracked event would be this:\n```javascript\n_ctrack.track(\"Checkout complete\", {\n            \"Item1\": \"4$\",\n            \"Item2\": \"7$\"});\n```\n\n#### Step 4: Track time spent in your product\nTracking the time spent on a page can be done using the following snippet:\n```javascript\n<script type=\"text/javascript\">\n    _ctrack.trackTime(true,\n        {\n          module: 'blog'\n        }\n    );\n</script>\n```\nwhere `module` represents the name you give to that specific page. The time in product for a user is tracked if one of the actions is detected: mouse move, click, scroll or keyboard input. If in the default idle time of `60` seconds no action is detected the tracking of time is stopped.\nThe default idle time can be changed by adding a new field in the JSON object for the `trackTime` function:\n```javascript\n<script type=\"text/javascript\">\n    _ctrack.trackTime(true,\n        {\n          module: 'blog',\n          idleTimer: 30\n        }\n    );\n</script>\n```\nOn pages that you don't want to track the time don't include the function `trackTime`. If your application is a SPA (single-page application) and you don't want to track a specific page you'll have to stop the tracking using the function `stopTrackTime`:\n```javascript\n<script type=\"text/javascript\">\n    _ctrack.stopTrackTime();\n</script>\n```\n\n#### Step 5: Create or update people / companies\nIn order to be able to the create/update people and/or companies through the JS snippet 2 different options have to be turned on:\n- one is from within the app at [Settings -> Developers -> JS snippet](https://app.custify.com/settings/developer/js-snippet) where you have to toggle ON the setting `Allow creating/updating people and companies via the JS snippet`, otherwise calls will be rejected with a HTTP 403 Forbidden code\n- one in the JS snippet code where you need to set the `createOrUpdateEntities` to `true` via the `setOptions` method **before** doing the `identify` call\n  ```javascript\n  <script type=\"text/javascript\">\n      _ctrack.setOptions({\n          \u201ccreateOrUpdateEntities\u201d: true\n      });\n  </script>\n  ```\n\nIn order to send entities to Custify, you need to amend the `_ctrack.identify()` call as it follows - adding the 2nd parameter to the call, where you include the entity attributes:\n\n```\n_ctrack.identify(\n  {\n      userId: 'USER_ID', // Your Id of the user\n      email: 'USER_EMAIL', // Email of the user\n      company_id: 'COMPANY_ID' // Your Id of the company\n  },\n  {\n      // The People entity within Custify\n      user: {\n          name: \"John Doe\",\n          email: 'john.doe@example.com', //if provided will overwrite the one on top, if not we use the one on top\n          unsubscribed_from_emails: false, //example of default attribute\n          custom_attributes: { //an object of custom_attributes, as described in the People Creation API\n              attr_1: \"test\",\n              attr_2: 123,\n              ...\n          }\n      },\n      // The Company entity within Custify\n      company: {\n          name: \"ACME Corporation\",\n          monthly_revenue: 10000,\n          custom_attributes: {\n              has_employees: false,\n              employees_number: 0,\n              owner: \"Road Runner\",\n              ...\n          }\n      }\n  }\n);\n```\n\nIf a `company` entity will be sent, then a Company record will be created or updated, depending on the `company_id` provided. If a `user` entity will be sent, then a People record will be created or updated, depending on the `user_id` provided. If there is a `user` entity sent and also a `company_id` specified in the first parameter of the identify call, then the user will be linked to that company (if it exists), no matter if a `company` entity is also provided or not.\n\n#### Step 6: Trigger in-app survey\nIn order to be able to trigger a in-app survey in your application through the JS snippet following things must happen:\n- update/install your JS snippet code to the latest version so that you can call the new functions `triggerPendingAction` and `closePendingAction` like in [Settings -> Developers -> JS snippet](https://app.custify.com/settings/developer/js-snippet)\n- request your CSM to get activated this option\n- after this option is activated for your account you can define a playbook that triggers the in-app survey step for certain companies/people\n- on the pages where you want to display the in-app survey, just trigger the `triggerPendingAction` function of the JS Snippet as such `_ctrack.triggerPendingAction()`, which will check the Custify backend for any actions available for the previously identified user (and company) that were set through the `_ctrack.idenfify()` call. Can be triggered on a page load or on a button click (or any valid action).\n- the HTML code of the in-app area has the following structure, but the exact styles (which are added inline) depend on the settings made in the Playbook step (where you can select the survey placement, the number of times it will be displayed and the number of days the survey will be available):\n```\n<div class=\"custify-in-app-container-outter\">\n  <div class=\"custify-in-app-container-inner\">\n    <iframe class=\"custify-in-app-iframe\"></iframe>\n    <div class=\"custify-in-app-close\">Close</div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n- if you want, you can further customize the look, feel and placement of the survey using the CSS classes provided, but for some properties using `!important` might be required.\n",
    "license": {
      "name": "Privacy Policy",
      "url": "https://www.custify.com/privacy"
    },
    "termsOfService": "https://www.custify.com/terms",
    "title": "Custify App",
    "version": "1.5.7",
    "x-logo": {
      "url": "https://docs.custify.com/images/logo.png"
    },
    "x-jentic-source-url": "https://docs.custify.com/openapi.yaml"
  },
  "openapi": "3.0.0",
  "paths": {
    "/batch": {
      "post": {
        "description": "You can send batch requests for creating/updating people or companies, for creating events or custom data. The requests can be processes synchronous or asynchronous based on the value sent in the request. The default processing is asynchronous.\nFor asynchronous jobs you can have a return job id which can be used to retrieve the status of the processing. If synchronous is set to true then the maximum number of jobs you can provide is 3. If synchronous is set to false you can provide maximum 100 jobs.\nThe jobs can be mixed (for people, companies, events or custom data). The return job id is kept for 6 hours after the last job in the batch is processed. The payload of the job depends of the type of job and should contain data in the same format as when creating/updating people, companies or events.\nFor custom data the payload should look like:\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"custom-data\",\n  \"payload\": {\n    \"entity\": \"65240f85e2a675bd3090a3d3\",\n    \"entityModel\": \"Company\",\n    \"data_type\": \"invoice\",\n    \"data_id\": \"INV_003\",\n    \"data\": {\n        \"amount\": 175,\n        \"invoiced_at\": \"2023-02-02T00:00:00Z\",\n        \"is_paid\": false,\n        \"product_name\": \"bronze_plan\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\nAlternatively, if you don't know the Custify entity ID you can send the `company_id` or `user_id` from your system by replacing field `entity` in the payload.\n",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Batch"
              }
            }
          },
          "description": "Batch request object",
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "202": {
            "description": "Successful operation"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/AccessForbidden"
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Some other error occurred"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Send batch requests",
        "tags": [
          "Batch"
        ],
        "x-code-samples": [
          {
            "lang": "Curl",
            "source": "curl 'https://api.custify.com/batch' \\\n -X POST \\\n -H 'Authorization: Bearer <Your access token>' \\\n -H 'Accept: application/json' \\\n -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d ' \n{\n  \"jobs\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"people\",\n      \"payload\": {\n        \"name\": \"John Doe\",\n        \"user_id\": \"batch_1\",\n        \"email\": \"john.doe@outlook.com\"\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"synchronous\": false,\n  \"returnJobId\": \"35757461-c988-5508-9f80-68bd45a99bf9\"\n}'"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "/batch/id": {
      "get": {
        "description": "Get status and results of the batch processing by provinding a 'returnJobId'.\n",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/batchJobId"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful operation"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/AccessForbidden"
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Some other error occurred"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Get batch job status",
        "tags": [
          "Batch"
        ],
        "x-code-samples": [
          {
            "lang": "Curl",
            "source": "curl 'https://api.custify.com/batch/id\\\n -X GET \\\n -H 'Authorization: Bearer <Your access token>' \\\n -H 'Accept: application/json' \\\n -H 'Content-Type: application/json'"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "/calculated_metric": {
      "get": {
        "description": "List calculated metrics. To list all the calculated metrics send a `GET` request to [https://api.custify.com/calculated_metric](https://api.custify.com/calculated_metric). To get calculated metrics for company/people send a `GET` request to [https://api.custify.com/calculated_metric?type=:type](https://api.custify.com/calculated_metric?type=:type). Default type is `company`.\nTo get a specific calculated metric send a `GET` request to [https://api.custify.com/calculated_metric/:id](https://api.custify.com/calculated_metric/:id).\n",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/itemsPerPageMax50"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/pageParam"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/sortingParam"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/typeParam"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "properties": {
                    "calculated_metrics": {
                      "description": "An array of objects with the details of the calculated metrics",
                      "items": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CalculatedMetricsListing"
                      },
                      "type": "array"
                    },
                    "total": {
                      "description": "Total number of calculated metrics",
                      "example": 1,
                      "type": "integer"
                    }
                  },
                  "type": "object"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful operation"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/AccessForbidden"
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Some other error occurred"
          }
        },
        "summary": "List calculated metrics",
        "tags": [
          "Calculated Metrics"
        ],
        "x-code-samples": [
          {
            "lang": "Curl",
            "source": "curl 'https://api.custify.com/calculated_metric?itemsPerPage=20&page=1' \\\n -X GET \\\n -H 'Authorization: Bearer <Your access token>' \\\n -H 'Accept: application/json' \\\n -H 'Content-Type: application/json'"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "/calendar/meeting": {
      "get": {
        "description": "List meetings. To list all the meetings send a `GET` request to [https://api.custify.com/calendar/meeting](https://api.custify.com/calendar/meeting).\nYou can send additional query params to filter or paginate results, like:\n- `company_id` (your internal company ID) - filters meetings by which company/companies they are assigned to.\n- `user_id` (your internal user ID) or `email` - filters meetings by which people they are assigned to.\n\nAlso you can filter meetings for companies/people by sending a `GET` request to [https://api.custify.com/calendar/meeting/:entityType/:entityId](https://api.custify.com/calendar/meeting/:entityType/:entityId) \nwhere `entityType` is the type of the entity (`company` or `people`) and `entityId` is the Custify internal ID of the entity.\n",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/itemsPerPageMax50"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/pageParam"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/sortingParam"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "properties": {
                    "meetings": {
                      "description": "An array of objects with the details of the meetings",
                      "items": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/schemas/MeetingsListing"
                      },
                      "type": "array"
                    },
                    "total": {
                      "description": "Total number of meetings",
                      "example": 1,
                      "type": "integer"
                    }
                  },
                  "type": "object"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful operation"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/AccessForbidden"
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Some other error occurred"
          }
        },
        "summary": "List meetings",
        "tags": [
          "Meetings"
        ],
        "x-code-samples": [
          {
            "lang": "Curl",
            "source": "curl 'https://api.custify.com/calendar/meeting?itemsPerPage=20&page=1' \\\n -X GET \\\n -H 'Authorization: Bearer <Your access token>' \\\n -H 'Accept: application/json' \\\n -H 'Content-Type: application/json'"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "/comment/{entityModel}/{entity}": {
      "get": {
        "description": "List the comments.\n",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/itemsPerPageMax50"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/pageParam"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/sortParam"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/orderParam"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "properties": {
                    "comments": {
                      "description": "An array of objects with the details of the comments",
                      "items": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CommentListing"
                      },
                      "type": "array"
                    },
                    "total": {
                      "description": "Total number of comments",
                      "example": 15,
                      "type": "integer"
                    }
                  },
                  "type": "object"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful operation"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/AccessForbidden"
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Some other error occurred"
          }
        },
        "summary": "List the comments",
        "tags": [
          "Comments"
        ],
        "x-code-samples": [
          {
            "lang": "Curl",
            "source": "curl 'https://api.custify.com/comment/:entityModel/:entity?itemsPerPage=20&page=1' \\\n -X GET \\\n -H 'Authorization: Bearer <Your access token>' \\\n -H 'Accept: application/json' \\\n -H 'Content-Type: application/json'"
          }
        ]
      },
      "post": {
        "description": "You can create a new comment or update an existing one by sending a POST request to [https://api.custify.com/comment/{entityModel}/{entity}](https://api.custify.com/comment/{entityModel}/{entity}), , where {entityModel} is 'Note' or 'Task', depending on the type of entity you are adding the comment to and {entity} is the Custify internal `id` of the Note or Task.\n",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/entityModelComment"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/entity"
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Comment"
              }
            }
          },
          "description": "Comment request object",
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CommentListing"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful operation"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/AccessForbidden"
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Some other error occurred"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Create or update a comment",
        "tags": [
          "Comments"
        ],
        "x-code-samples": [
          {
            "lang": "Curl",
            "source": "curl 'https://api.custify.com/comment/:entityModel/:entity' \\\n -X POST \\\n -H 'Authorization: Bearer <Your access token>' \\\n -H 'Accept: application/json' \\\n -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d ' \n{\n  \"text\": \"First comment\"\n}'"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "/company": {
      "delete": {
        "description": "Companies can be deleted by sending a DELETE request to the entry's URL using the Custify *id* field as part of the path\n- `https://api.custify.com/company/{id}`\n\nAlternatively, you can delete a company by sending a DELETE request using the *company_id* as query parameter\n- `https://api.custify.com/company?company_id={company_id}`\n\nNote that this function permanently deletes any records, such as events, and any other data within Custify. It also represents the GDPR compliance on your end and our end. You have to call this function if a company requests to be deleted from all your records (\"forget me\").\n",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/resourceId"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful operation"
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Bad request (invalid request syntax)"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/AccessForbidden"
          },
          "404": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/NotFound"
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Some other error occurred"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Delete company",
        "tags": [
          "Company"
        ],
        "x-code-samples": [
          {
            "lang": "Curl",
            "source": "curl 'https://api.custify.com/company/5d1eea314ce8477adf5af46c' \\\n -X DELETE \\\n -H 'Authorization: Bearer <Your access token>' \\\n -H 'Accept: application/json' \\\n -H 'Content-Type: application/json'"
          }
        ]
      },
      "post": {
        "description": "Companies can be created or updated via a POST to https://api.custify.com/company, which accepts a JSON object describing the company.\nCompanies are looked up via `id` or `company_id` - if it's not found via both parameters, the new company will be created. If a company is found, it will be updated.\n\nNote that the `company_id` field itself cannot be updated through the API.\n\nWhen submitting custom attributes of type `User` you can specify the Custify internal ID of the user or the email address. Examples:\n```json\n{\n  \"company_id\": \"1\",\n  \"custom_attributes\": {\n    \"user_type_field\": \"531ee472cce572a6ec000006\"\n  }\n}\n```\nor\n\n```json\n{\n  \"company_id\": \"1\",\n  \"custom_attributes\": {\n    \"user_type_field\": \"john.doe@example.com\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Associate a company with another company\nOnce a company is assigned to another company, the events generated by the people that are part of the \"child\" company are also associated with the \"parent\" company.\nTo associate a company with another company, send a POST request with the following JSON body:\n```json\n{\n  \"company_id\": \"1\",\n  \"parent_companies\": [\n    {\n      \"company_id\" : \"2\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\nwhere `company_id` is *your internal ID* of the company and was specified through the company API call. If you want to use the Custify internal ID, send a POST with the following JSON body:\n```json\n{\n  \"company_id\": \"1\",\n  \"parent_companies\": [\n    {\n      \"id\" : \"531ee472cce572a6ec000006\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### Remove a company from 'parent_companies' of another company\nTo remove a company from 'parent_companies' of another company, send a POST request with the following JSON body:\n```json\n{\n  \"company_id\": \"1\",\n  \"parent_companies\": [\n    {\n      \"company_id\" : \"2\",\n      \"remove\" : true\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\nwhere `company_id` is *your internal ID* of the company and was specified through the company API call. If you want to use the Custify internal ID, send a POST with the following JSON body:\n```json\n{\n  \"company_id\": \"1\",\n  \"companies\": [\n    {\n      \"id\" : \"531ee472cce572a6ec000006\",\n      \"remove\" : true\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### Insert/update a field of type 'Currency'\nTo insert/update a field of type 'Currency', send a POST request with the following JSON body:\n```json\n{\n  \"company_id\": \"1\",\n  \"custom_attributes\": {\n      \"currency_field\": {\n        \"value\": 100,\n        \"currency\": \"USD\"\n      }\n  }\n}\n```\n",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Company"
              }
            }
          },
          "description": "Created company object",
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful operation"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/AccessForbidden"
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Company not found"
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Some other error occurred"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Create or update a company",
        "tags": [
          "Company"
        ],
        "x-code-samples": [
          {
            "lang": "Curl",
            "source": "curl 'https://api.custify.com/company' \\\n -X POST \\\n -H 'Authorization: Bearer <Your access token>' \\\n -H 'Accept: application/json' \\\n -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d ' \n{\n  \"company_id\": 6,\n  \"name\": \"Pizzeria Presto\",\n  \"signed_up_at\": \"2019-05-30T12:00:00.000Z\",\n  \"size\": 15,\n  \"website\": \"www.pizzeriapresto.com\",\n  \"industry\": \"Restaurant\",\n  \"monthly_revenue\": 1234567,\n  \"churned\": false,\n  \"custom_attributes\": {\n    \"restaurants\": 5,\n    \"custom\": \"template\"\n  }\n}'"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "/company/all": {
      "get": {
        "description": "You can fetch a list of companies. The list, by default, is sorted by the `signed_up_at` field and in `descending` order, with the most recent signups first.\n### Filtering companies\nIf you want to apply filters to the `/company/all` endpoint, you would need to send the `filters` query parameter as an URL-encoded array of objects as follows:\n```json\n  [\n      {\n        fieldName: \"name\",\n        fieldType: \"String\",\n        filterType: \"contains\",\n        filterValue: \"a\"\n      }\n  ]\n```\n\nThe operator used between the different conditions passed will be **AND**, so the returned entities must fulfill all the conditions sent in the filters array. Also, the same field can be sent multiple times if for example you want to filter for names that start with A and also contain XY.\n\nFor the `fieldName` property, you should send it formatted as it follows:\n- If it is a default attribute, send just the name: `name`, `size`, `created_at`, `owners_csm`, etc\n- If it is a custom attribute, send it using dot-notation, as follows: `custom_attributes.myAttribute`, `custom_attributes.deal_stage`, etc\n- If you want to filter by tag, sent the name `tags`\n- If you want to filter by a calculated metric, sent it as `metrics.calculated_metrics.CALCULATED_METRIC_ID`, example `metrics.calculated_metrics.5fa5b24f584088153f7fd825`\n- If you want to filter by a health score, send it as `metrics.health_scores.HEALTH_SCORE_ID`, example `metrics.health_scores.5f86fee26e8f7c489b28dd03`\n\nPossible values for `fieldType`, with associated values for the other properties as well:\n- **Number**:\n    - Available for all numerical default and custom attributes as well as calculated metrics and health scores and has the following possible `filterType` values:\n        - `greater` - the value of the attribute/metric is greater than the value provided in the `filterValue` field\n        - `lower` - the value of the attribute/metric is lower than the value provided in the `filterValue` field\n        - `is` - the value of the attribute/metric is equal to the value provided in the `filterValue` field\n        - `is_not` - the value of the attribute/metric is different from the value provided in the `filterValue` field\n        - `is_unknown` - the attribute/metric does not exist on the entity. The `filterValue` can be sent as either NULL or empty string\n        - `any_value` - the attribute/metric exists on the entity and has any value. The `filterValue` can be sent as either NULL or empty string\n    - If the `fieldName` is a health score, there are 3 additional `filterType` options that can be used. For all of them the `filterValue` should be either an empty string or NULL:\n        - `is_bad` - the health score is bad, meaning the value of the health score is in the red area as defined in the health score settings\n        - `is_average` - the health score is average, meaning the value of the health score is in the orange area as defined in the health score settings\n        - `is_good` - the health score is good, meaning the value of the health score is in the green area as defined in the health score settings\n- **String**:\n    - Available for all textual default and custom attributes and has the following possible `filterType` values:\n        - `is` - the value of the attribute is equal to the value provided in the `filterValue` field\n        - `is_not` - the value of the attribute is different from the value provided in the `filterValue` field\n        - `starts_with` - the value of the attribute starts with the value provided in `filterValue`\n        - `ends_with` - the value of the attribute ends with the value provided in `filterValue`\n        - `contains` - the value of the attribute contains the value provided in `filterValue`\n        - `does_not_contain` - the value of the attribute does not contain the value provided in `filterValue`\n        - `is_unknown` - the attribute/metric does not exist on the entity. The `filterValue` can be sent as either NULL or empty string\n        - `any_value` - the attribute/metric exists on the entity and has any value. The `filterValue` can be sent as either NULL or empty string\n    - Should also be used when the `fieldName` is `owners_csm` or `owners_account` (when filtering by Company CSM or Company Account Manager), but then the possible `filterType` values are:\n        - `is` - in this particular case the `filterValue` should contain the Custify User ID of the CSM / Account Manager\n        - `is_unknown` - means that the company does not have a CSM / Account Manager\n- **User**:\n    - Available for attributes of type `User` (created using Event-attribute editor) and has the following possible `filterType` values:\n        - `is` - the value of the attribute is equal to the value provided in the `filterValue` field and should contain the Custify User ID of the user\n        - `is_unknown` - the attribute does not exist on the entity. The `filterValue` can be sent as either NULL or empty string\n- **Date**:\n    - Available for all date default and custom attributes and has the following possible values for `filterType`:\n        - `more_than` - means that the value of the attribute is more than X (where X is the value provided in `filterValue` - which is a Number) days ago\n        - `exactly` - means that the value of the attribute is exactly X (where X is the value provided in `filterValue` - which is a Number) days ago\n        - `less_than` - means that the value of the attribute is less than X (where X is the value provided in `filterValue` - which is a Number) days ago\n        - `after` - means that the value of the attribute is after the date X (where X is the value provided in `filterValue` in the `YYYY-MM-DD` format)\n        - `on`  - means that the value of the attribute is on the date X (where X is the value provided in `filterValue` in the `YYYY-MM-DD` format)\n        - `before`  - means that the value of the attribute is before the date X (where X is the value provided in `filterValue` in the `YYYY-MM-DD` format)\n        - `between`  - means that the value of the attribute is between the dates X and Y (where X and Y are the value provided in `filterValue` as an array `[X,Y]` each in the `YYYY-MM-DD` format)\n- **Boolean**:\n    - Available for all boolean default and custom attributes and has the following possible values for `filterType`. Also, for Boolean fields the `filterValue` should always be empty string or NULL:\n        - `true` - the value of the attribute is TRUE\n        - `false` - the value of the attribute is FALSE\n        - `is_unknown` - the attribute does not exist on the entity\n        - `any_value` - the attribute exists on the entity and has any value\n- **Tag**:\n    - This is the `fieldType` that must be used when filtering for the `tags` field and the following options for `filterType` are available\n        - `is_in` - the `filterValue` must be the Custify ID of a tag and will return entities that have that tag applied\n        - `is_not_in` - the `filterValue` must be the Custify ID of a tag and will return entities that do not have that tag applied\n        - `is_unknown` - the `filterValue` should be either NULL or an empty string and will return entities that have no tags applied to them\n- **Company**:\n    - This is the `fieldType` that must be used when filtering on `People` to retrieve people that are part of the specified company. The following options for `filterType` are available\n        - `is_in` - the `filterValue` must be the Custify ID of a company and will return entities that match the applied filter\n        - `is_unknown` - the `filterValue` should be either NULL or an empty string and will return entities that match the applied filter\n\nFiltering for `Parent companies` can be done using the following values for the fields:\n- `fieldName` should be `parent_companies`\n- `fieldType` should be `String`\n- `filterType` should have one of the options:\n    - `is_descendant` - will return entities that are descendants (children, grand-children, etc...) of the company set in the `filterValue` field\n    - `is_in` - will return entities that are children of the company set in the `filterValue` field\n- `filterValue` should be the Custify internal ID of the company for which the filtering values is applied.\n### Filtering properties\nIf you want to apply filters to the response from `/company/all` endpoint, you would need to send the `properties` query parameter as an URL-encoded array of fields to be returned.\nSome default properties are available for all entities: `id`, `name`, `created_at` and `updated_at`.\n",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/itemsPerPageMax200"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/pageParam"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/sortingParam"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/filteringParam"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/includeSegmentsParam"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/filteringProperties"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful operation"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/AccessForbidden"
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Some other error occurred"
          }
        },
        "summary": "List companies",
        "tags": [
          "Company"
        ],
        "x-code-samples": [
          {
            "lang": "Curl",
            "source": "curl 'https://api.custify.com/company/all?itemsPerPage=10&page=7' \\\n -X GET \\\n -H 'Authorization: Bearer <Your access token>' \\\n -H 'Accept: application/json' \\\n -H 'Content-Type: application/json'"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "/company/people/{id}": {
      "get": {
        "description": "The people belonging to a company can be listed by sending a GET request to https://api.custify.com/company/people/{id}, where {id} is the Custify internal ID of the company.\n",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful operation"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/AccessForbidden"
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Param ID is missing or invalid"
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Some other error occurred"
          }
        },
        "summary": "List Company People",
        "tags": [
          "Company"
        ],
        "x-code-samples": [
          {
            "lang": "Curl",
            "source": "curl 'https://api.custify.com/company/people/5b9f95d838ab5e09b8ed66cb' \\\n -X GET \\\n -H 'Authorization: Bearer <Your access token>' \\\n -H 'Accept: application/json' \\\n -H 'Content-Type: application/json'"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "/company/{id}": {
      "get": {
        "description": "You can view a company\u2019s details by sending a GET request to [https://api.custify.com/company/{id}](https://api.custify.com/company/{id}), where {id} is the value of the company's `id` field. Companies can also be fetched using a `company_id` parameter in the URL.\nIf the company has set user type attributes, like the default ones `owners_csm` or `owners_account`, or user defined attributes, like `user_type_field`, those will be enhanced in the response with the email and the name of the user, like `{attribute}_email` and `{attribute}_name`.\nIf the user above has set `user custom attributes` those will be enhanced in the response with the value of the custom attribute, like `{attribute}_attributes`, if you'll pass in the query params of the request the field `includeUserAttributes` with the value of `true`. This field will be of type `object` and will contain all the custom attributes of the user.\nIf you want to apply filters to the response from `/company/{id}` endpoint, you would need to send the `properties` query parameter as an URL-encoded array of fields to be returned.\nSome default properties are available for all entities: `id`, `name`, `created_at` and `updated_at`.\n",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/resourceIdOptional"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/companyIdParam"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/includeSegmentsParam"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/filteringProperties"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful operation"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/AccessForbidden"
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Param provided is missing or invalid"
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Some other error occurred"
          }
        },
        "summary": "View company",
        "tags": [
          "Company"
        ],
        "x-code-samples": [
          {
            "lang": "Curl",
            "source": "curl 'https://api.custify.com/company/5d26f09c5c629e342bf47ff3' \\\n -X GET \\\n -H 'Authorization: Bearer <Your access token>' \\\n -H 'Accept: application/json' \\\n -H 'Content-Type: application/json'"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "/csat_score/{entity}": {
      "post": {
        "description": "You can assign a CSAT score to a people by sending a POST request to [https://api.custify.com/csat_score/{entity}](https://api.custify.com/csat_score/{entity}), where {entity} is the Custify internal `id` of the People.\nAlternatively, you can assign a CSAT score to a people by sending a POST request to:\n- [https://api.custify.com/csat_score?email=john.doe@custify.com](https://api.custify.com/csat_score?email=john.doe@custify.com) or\n- [https://api.custify.com/csat_score?user_id=123](https://api.custify.com/csat_score?user_id=123) where `user_id` is the ID from your system.\nYou can also assign the CSAT score to a survey by sending a POST request to [https://api.custify.com/csat_score?{surveyId=xyz}](https://api.custify.com/csat_score?{surveyId=xyz}), where {surveyId} is the Custify internal `id` of the Survey.\n\nIn the body of the request you can send the CSAT score (`score`), a comment (`comment`) and the date of the CSAT score (`submittedAt`). Only the field `score` is required. If you don't provide the `submittedAt` field it will be saved the current UTC time.\nIf the people for which you're sending the CSAT score already has saved a CSAT score, it will be kept the newest one based on the `submittedAt` date field.\nIf the people you're assigning the CSAT score is linked to a company then also the company gets assigned a CSAT score which is calculated as the arithmetic mean (rounded to the nearest integer) of all people's CSAT scores that are linked to the company.\n",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/entity"
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CSATScore"
              }
            }
          },
          "description": "CSAT score request object",
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful operation"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/AccessForbidden"
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Some other error occurred"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Assign a CSAT score to a people",
        "tags": [
          "CSATScore"
        ],
        "x-code-samples": [
          {
            "lang": "Curl",
            "source": "curl 'https://api.custify.com/csat_score/:entity' \\\n -X POST \\\n -H 'Authorization: Bearer <Your access token>' \\\n -H 'Accept: application/json' \\\n -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d ' \n{\n  \"score\": 5,\n  \"comment\": \"Very satisfied\",\n  \"submittedAt\": \"2021-04-10T12:00:00.000Z\"\n}'"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "/custom_data/{entityModel}/{entity}": {
      "delete": {
        "description": "You can delete one or more custom data objects by sending a DELETE request to:\n- [https://api.custify.com/custom_data/{entityModel}/{entity}](https://api.custify.com/custom_data/{entityModel}/{entity}), where {entityModel} is 'companies' or 'people', depending on the type of entity you are adding the custom data object to and {entity} is the Custify internal `id` of the Company or People or\n- [https://api.custify.com/custom_data/{entityModel}](https://api.custify.com/custom_data/{entityModel}), where {entityModel} is 'companies' or 'people', depending on the type of entity you are adding the custom data object to\n\nYou can also enhance the request by sending in the query params {data_type} and/or {data_id}. If you use the second request type you must send as a query param also {company_id} or {user_id} (depending on the type of entity of custom data object) where `company_id` or `user_id` is the entity ID from your own system.\n",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/entityModel"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/entityNotRequired"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful operation"
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Bad request (invalid request syntax)"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/AccessForbidden"
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Some other error occurred"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Delete a custom data object",
        "tags": [
          "CustomData"
        ],
        "x-code-samples": [
          {
            "lang": "Curl",
            "source": "curl 'https://api.custify.com/custom_data/:entityModel/:entity' \\\n -X DELETE \\\n -H 'Authorization: Bearer <Your access token>' \\\n -H 'Accept: application/json'"
          }
        ]
      },
      "get": {
        "description": "You can list custom data objects by sending a GET request to [https://api.custify.com/custom_data/{entityModel}/{entity}](https://api.custify.com/custom_data/{entityModel}/{entity}), where {entityModel} is 'companies' or 'people', depending on the type of entity you are adding the custom data object to and {entity} is the Custify internal `id` of the Company or People.\nAlternatively, you can list custom data objects by sending a GET request to:\n- [https://api.custify.com/custom_data/{entityModel}?company_id=123](https://api.custify.com/custom_data/{entityModel}?company_id=123) for `{entityModel}=companies` or\n- [https://api.custify.com/custom_data/{entityModel}?user_id=123](https://api.custify.com/custom_data/{entityModel}?user_id=123) for `{entityModel}=people`\n\nwhere `company_id` or `user_id` is the entity ID from your own system. You can also filter the custom data objects by sending the query params {data_type} and/or {data_id} (ex. [https://api.custify.com/custom_data/{entityModel}/{entity}](https://api.custify.com/custom_data/{entityModel}/{entity}?data_type=invoice&data_id=invoice1]).\n",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/entityModel"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/entityNotRequired"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "properties": {
                    "data_type_1": {
                      "description": "An array of objects with the details of the custom data",
                      "items": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CustomDataListing"
                      },
                      "type": "array"
                    },
                    "data_type_2": {
                      "description": "An array of objects with the details of the custom data",
                      "items": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CustomDataListing"
                      },
                      "type": "array"
                    }
                  },
                  "type": "object"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful operation"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/AccessForbidden"
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Some other error occurred"
          }
        },
        "summary": "List custom data objects",
        "tags": [
          "CustomData"
        ],
        "x-code-samples": [
          {
            "lang": "Curl",
            "source": "curl 'https://api.custify.com/custom_data/:entityModel/:entity' \\\n -X GET \\\n -H 'Authorization: Bearer <Your access token>' \\\n -H 'Accept: application/json' \\\n'"
          }
        ]
      },
      "post": {
        "description": "You can add new custom data objects or update existing ones by sending a POST request to [https://api.custify.com/custom_data/{entityModel}/{entity}](https://api.custify.com/custom_data/{entityModel}/{entity}), where {entityModel} is 'companies' or 'people', depending on the type of entity you are adding the custom data object to and {entity} is the Custify internal `id` of the Company or People.\nAlternatively, you can add new custom data objects or update existing ones by sending a POST request to:\n- [https://api.custify.com/custom_data/{entityModel}?company_id=123](https://api.custify.com/custom_data/{entityModel}?company_id=123) for `{entityModel}=companies` or\n- [https://api.custify.com/custom_data/{entityModel}?user_id=123](https://api.custify.com/custom_data/{entityModel}?user_id=123) for `{entityModel}=people`\n\nwhere `company_id` or `user_id` is the entity ID from your own system.\n\nNote that the combination of `data_type` and `data_id` represents an unique index and triggers the creation or updating of a custom data object.\n\nYou can also send bulk custom data objects for the current entity by sending an array of the Custom data request objects.\n",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/entityModel"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/entityNotRequired"
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CustomData"
              }
            }
          },
          "description": "Custom data request object",
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful operation"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/AccessForbidden"
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Some other error occurred"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Add or update a custom data object",
        "tags": [
          "CustomData"
        ],
        "x-code-samples": [
          {
            "lang": "Curl",
            "source": "curl 'https://api.custify.com/custom_data/:entityModel/:entity' \\\n -X POST \\\n -H 'Authorization: Bearer <Your access token>' \\\n -H 'Accept: application/json' \\\n -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d ' \n{\n  \"data_type\": \"invoice\",\n  \"data_id\": \"INV_001\",\n  \"data\": {}\n}'"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "/event": {
      "post": {
        "description": "Submit events via a POST method to https://api.custify.com/event, which accepts a JSON object describing the event.\n\nNote that the following lookup order applies when inserting events for a people: `user_id` then `email`. This results in the following logic:\n - `user_id` match: the `email` will be ignored if it is passed.\n - `email` match: the `user_id` is missing.\n\nIf submitting events for a people the company ID field is optional, it is only needed if you have people that are assigned to several companies at the same time. Use it then, to specify the company that this event should be counted for.\n\nWhen submitting \u201ccompany-only\u201d events you have to specify the `company_id` field. The `user_id` field should not be present in this case.\n",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Event"
              }
            }
          },
          "description": "Created event object",
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "202": {
            "description": "Successful operation"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/AccessForbidden"
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "People not found"
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Some other error occurred"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Insert events",
        "tags": [
          "Event"
        ],
        "x-code-samples": [
          {
            "lang": "Curl",
            "source": "curl 'https://api.custify.com/event' \\\n -X POST \\\n -H 'Authorization: Bearer <Your access token>' \\\n -H 'Accept: application/json' \\\n -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d ' \n{\n  \"name\": \"login\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2019-05-30T12:00:00.000Z\",\n  \"user_id\": \"1\",\n  \"email\": \"test@example.org\",\n \"deduplication_id\": \"5d95ecc9749204521d2e7945\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"email\": \"john@example.org\",\n    \"code\": \"ABCDEF\"\n  }\n}'"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "/file": {
      "get": {
        "description": "You can list files for a Company or a People by sending a GET request to [https://api.custify.com/file](https://api.custify.com/file). You can send additional query params to filter or paginate results.\n",
