      }
    },
    "/note/{entityId}": {
      "get": {
        "description": "You can fetch a list of notes. The list, by default, is sorted by `sticky` field when retrieving notes for just one entity and by `created_at` field when retrieving all notes. Also, by default, the order is `descending`, with the most recent notes first.\nYou can request notes for a specific entity by sending a GET request to [https://api.custify.com/note/{entityId}](https://api.custify.com/note/{entityId}), where {entityId} is Custify internal `id`.\n### Filtering notes\nIf you want to apply filters to this endpoint, you would need to send the `filters` query parameter as an URL-encoded array of objects as follows:\n```json\n[\n  {\n    field: \"createdByEntity\", //the field to filter by\n    values: ['629dfbc3e827ed3cd0de1a53',\u2026] //the values\n  },\n  ...\n]\n```\nThe logic applied to filtering is `OR` between different values for the same field and `AND` between different fields, for example:\n```\n(createdByEntity='value1' OR createdByEntity='value2') AND (tags='value3' OR tags='value4')\n```\n\nThe following fields can be filtered (including what can be sent in the values array):\n  - `createdByEntity` - filters notes by who/what they were created by. The allowed values are `api`, `playbook_{id}`, `user_{id}`, `integration_{id}` where `{id}` is the Custify ID of the entity (for playbook and user) \nor the name of the integration (like `hubspot`, `close`) that have created the note\n  - `tags` - filters notes by tags, the values being Custify IDs of Tags\n  - `mentioning` - filters notes by users mentioned in them, the values being Custify IDs of users\n\nExtra filtering can be archived by using the `searchTerm` query parameter and should be a string. This will filter notes by the text they contain or by the external ID if the note came from a integration.\n",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/limitParam"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/pageParam"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/sortParam"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/orderParam"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful operation"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/AccessForbidden"
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Some other error occurred"
          }
        },
        "summary": "List notes",
        "tags": [
          "Note"
        ],
        "x-code-samples": [
          {
            "lang": "Curl",
            "source": "curl 'https://api.custify.com/note{/entityId}?itemsPerPage=10&page=7' \\\n -X GET \\\n -H 'Authorization: Bearer <Your access token>' \\\n -H 'Accept: application/json' \\\n -H 'Content-Type: application/json'"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "/note/{id}": {
      "post": {
        "description": "You can create a new note or update an existing one by sending a POST request to [https://api.custify.com/note/{id}](https://api.custify.com/note/{id}), where {id} is the value of the Custify internal `id` of the note.\n",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/resourceIdOptional"
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Note"
              }
            }
          },
          "description": "Note request object",
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful operation"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/AccessForbidden"
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Some other error occurred"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Create or update a note",
        "tags": [
          "Note"
        ],
        "x-code-samples": [
          {
            "lang": "Curl",
            "source": "curl 'https://api.custify.com/note' \\\n -X POST \\\n -H 'Authorization: Bearer <Your access token>' \\\n -H 'Accept: application/json' \\\n -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d ' \n{\n  \"text\": \"First note\",\n  \"entity\": \"5ed60ea90494f32ff3959079\",\n  \"entityModel\": \"Company\",\n  \"sticky\": true\n}'"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "/nps_score/{entity}": {
      "post": {
        "description": "You can assign a nps score to a people by sending a POST request to [https://api.custify.com/nps_score/{entity}](https://api.custify.com/nps_score/{entity}), where {entity} is the Custify internal `id` of the People.\nAlternatively, you can assign a nps score to a people by sending a POST request to:\n- [https://api.custify.com/nps_score?email=john.doe@custify.com](https://api.custify.com/nps_score?email=john.doe@custify.com) or\n- [https://api.custify.com/nps_score?user_id=123](https://api.custify.com/nps_score?user_id=123) where `user_id` is the ID from your system.\nYou can also assign the nps score to a survey by sending a POST request to [https://api.custify.com/nps_score?{surveyId=xyz}](https://api.custify.com/nps_score?{surveyId=xyz}), where {surveyId} is the Custify internal `id` of the Survey.\n\nIn the body of the request you can send the NPS score (`score`), a comment (`comment`) and the date of the NPS score (`submittedAt`). Only the field `score` is required. If you don't provide the `submittedAt` field it will be saved the current UTC time.\nIf the people for which you're sending the NPS score already has saved a NPS score, it will be kept the newest one based on the `submittedAt` date field.\nIf the people you're assigning the NPS score is linked to a company then also the company gets assigned a NPS score which is calculated as the arithmetic mean (rounded to the nearest integer) of all people's NPS scores that are linked to the company.\n",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/entity"
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/NPSScore"
              }
            }
          },
          "description": "NPS score request object",
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful operation"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/AccessForbidden"
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Some other error occurred"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Assign a nps score to a people",
        "tags": [
          "NPSScore"
        ],
        "x-code-samples": [
          {
            "lang": "Curl",
            "source": "curl 'https://api.custify.com/nps_score/:entity' \\\n -X POST \\\n -H 'Authorization: Bearer <Your access token>' \\\n -H 'Accept: application/json' \\\n -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d ' \n{\n  \"score\": 9,\n  \"comment\": \"Almost perfect\",\n  \"submittedAt\": \"2021-04-10T12:00:00.000Z\"\n}'"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "/objective": {
      "get": {
        "description": "List objectives for a specific company. You must provide either the Custify internal ID of the company via the `company` query parameter, or your internal ID via the `company_id` query parameter.\n\nResults are paginated and sorted by `created_at` in descending order by default. You can use the `sort` and `order` query parameters to change the sorting. You can also use the `filters` query parameter to filter objectives by status, importance, risk, etc.\n",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/companyParam"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/companyIdParam"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/itemsPerPageMax50"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/pageParam"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/sortingParam"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/filteringParam"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "properties": {
                    "itemsPerPage": {
                      "description": "Number of items per page",
                      "example": 20,
                      "type": "integer"
                    },
                    "objectives": {
                      "description": "An array of objective objects",
                      "items": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ObjectiveListing"
                      },
                      "type": "array"
                    },
                    "page": {
                      "description": "Current page number",
                      "example": 1,
                      "type": "integer"
                    },
                    "total": {
                      "description": "Total number of objectives for this company",
                      "example": 5,
                      "type": "integer"
                    }
                  },
                  "type": "object"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful operation"
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Bad request - missing company or company_id query parameter"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/AccessForbidden"
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Company not found"
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Some other error occurred"
          }
        },
        "summary": "List customer objectives",
        "tags": [
          "Customer Objectives"
        ],
        "x-code-samples": [
          {
            "lang": "Curl",
            "source": "curl 'https://api.custify.com/objective?company_id=123&itemsPerPage=20&page=1' \\\n -X GET \\\n -H 'Authorization: Bearer <Your access token>' \\\n -H 'Accept: application/json' \\\n -H 'Content-Type: application/json'"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "/people": {
      "delete": {
        "description": "People can be deleted by sending a DELETE request to the entry's URL using the Custify *id* field as part of the path\n- `https://api.custify.com/people/{id}`\n\nAlternatively, you can delete people by sending a DELETE request using the *email* or *user_id* as query parameters\n- `https://api.custify.com/people?email={email}`\n- `https://api.custify.com/people?user_id={user_id}`\n\nNote that this function permanently deletes any records, such as events, and any other data within Custify. It also represents the GDPR compliance on your end and our end. You have to call this function if a person requests to be deleted from all your records (\"forget me\").\n",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/resourceIdOptional"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/userIdParam"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/emailParam"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful operation"
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Bad request (invalid request syntax)"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/AccessForbidden"
          },
          "404": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/NotFound"
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Some other error occurred"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Delete people",
        "tags": [
          "People"
        ],
        "x-code-samples": [
          {
            "lang": "Curl",
            "source": "curl 'https://api.custify.com/people?user_id=123' \\\n -X DELETE \\\n -H 'Authorization: Bearer <Your access token>' \\\n -H 'Accept: application/json' \\\n -H 'Content-Type: application/json'"
          }
        ]
      },
      "post": {
        "description": "People can be created or updated via a POST method to [https://api.custify.com/people](https://api.custify.com/people), which accepts a JSON object describing the people. People not found via email or user_id will be created, and those found will be updated if one of the attributes contains a new value or if you add a new attribute.\n\nNote that the following lookup order applies when updating people: first `id` (Custify internal ID), then `user_id` (your internal ID of the person), then `email`. This results in the following logic:\n- `id` is matched: the `user_id` and `email` will be updated if they\"re sent\n- `user_id` match: the `email` will be updated, the `id` is not updated\n- `email` match where no `user_id` set on the matching user: the `user_id` will be set to the value sent in the request, the `id` is not updated\n- `email` match where there is a `user_id` set on the matching user: a new unique record with new `id` will be created if a new value for `user_id` is sent in the request.\n\n### Associate people with a company\nThe assignment of people to companies should be done as soon as possible in your process; ideally right after creating the person entry. Once people are assigned to a company, the events they generate are also associated with that company.\nTo associate a company with a customer, send a POST request with the following JSON body:\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"531ee472cce572a6ec000005\",\n  \"companies\": [\n    {\n      \"company_id\" : \"366\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\nwhere `company_id` is *your internal ID* of the company and was specified through the company API call before. If you want to use the Custify internal ID, send a POST with the following JSON body:\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"531ee472cce572a6ec000005\",\n  \"companies\": [\n    {\n      \"id\" : \"531ee472cce572a6ec000006\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### Remove people from a company\nTo remove people from a company, send a POST request with the following JSON body:\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"531ee472cce572a6ec000005\",\n  \"companies\": [\n    {\n      \"company_id\" : \"3\",\n      \"remove\" : true\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\nwhere `company_id` is *your internal ID* of the company and was specified through the company API call before. If you want to use the Custify internal ID, send a POST with the following JSON body:\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"531ee472cce572a6ec000005\",\n  \"companies\": [\n    {\n      \"id\" : \"531ee472cce572a6ec000006\",\n      \"remove\" : true\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/resourceIdOptional"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/userIdParam"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/emailParam"
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/People"
              }
            }
          },
          "description": "Created people object",
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful operation"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/AccessForbidden"
          },
          "404": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/NotFound"
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Some other error occurred"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Create or update people",
        "tags": [
          "People"
        ],
        "x-code-samples": [
          {
            "lang": "Curl",
            "source": "curl 'https://api.custify.com/people' \\\n -X POST \\\n -H 'Authorization: Bearer <Your access token>' \\\n -H 'Accept: application/json' \\\n -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '\n{\n  \"user_id\": \"25\",\n  \"email\": \"john.doe@mail.com\",\n  \"phone\": \"+44 7911 123456\",\n  \"signed_up_at\": \"2019-05-30T12:00:00.000Z\",\n  \"name\": \"John Doe\",\n  \"session_count\": 2,\n  \"custom_attributes\": {\n    \"bool_paid_subscriber\": true,\n    \"int_team_mates\": 5,\n    \"string_plan\": \"advanced\",\n    \"date_example_date_at\": \"2019-06-30T12:00:00.000Z\"\n  },\n  \"unsubscribed_from_emails\": false,\n  \"unsubscribed_from_calls\": false\n }'"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "/people/all": {
      "get": {
        "description": "You can fetch a list of people. The list, by default, is sorted by the `signed_up_at` field and in `descending` order, with the most recent signups first.\n### Filtering people\nIf you want to apply filters to the `/people/all` endpoint, you would need to send the `filters` query parameter as an URL-encoded array of objects. You can follow the steps described when filtering [Companies](#tag/Company/paths/~1company~1all/get).\n### Filtering properties\nIf you want to apply filters to the response from `/people/all` endpoint, you would need to send the `properties` query parameter as an URL-encoded array of fields to be returned.\nSome default properties are available for all entities: `id`, `name`, `created_at` and `updated_at`.\n",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/itemsPerPageMax200"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/pageParam"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/sortingParam"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/filteringParam"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/includeSegmentsParam"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/filteringProperties"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful operation"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/AccessForbidden"
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Some other error occurred"
          }
        },
        "summary": "List people",
        "tags": [
          "People"
        ],
        "x-code-samples": [
          {
            "lang": "Curl",
            "source": "curl 'https://api.custify.com/people/all?itemsPerPage=10&page=7' \\\n -X GET \\\n -H 'Authorization: Bearer <Your access token>' \\\n -H 'Accept: application/json' \\\n -H 'Content-Type: application/json'"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "/people/tag": {
      "post": {
        "description": "Adding or removing a tag to or from a people. To add the tag you'll need to send the `type=\"add\"` and for removing you'll need to send the `type=\"remove\"`.",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/PeopleTag"
              }
            }
          },
          "description": "Add/remove tag to/from a people object",
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful operation"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/AccessForbidden"
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Some other error occurred"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Add/remove tag to/from a people",
        "tags": [
          "People"
        ],
        "x-code-samples": [
          {
            "lang": "Curl",
            "source": "curl 'https://api.custify.com/people/tag' \\\n -X POST \\\n -H 'Authorization: Bearer <Your access token>' \\\n -H 'Accept: application/json' \\\n -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '\n{\n  \"ids\": [\"5d402cf8c3a4c5578c9be5f4\", \"5d11c88ca6674a2541ade9b8\"],\n  \"type\": \"add\",\n  \"tag\": \"5d948817c5f9442ea5482321\"\n }'"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "/people/{id}": {
      "get": {
        "description": "You can view people\u2019s details by sending a GET request to [https://api.custify.com/people/{id}](https://api.custify.com/people/{id}), where {id} is the value of the person's `id` field. \nPeople can also be fetched using a `user_id` or `email` parameter in the URL. If you want to apply filters to the response from `/people/{id}` endpoint, you would need to send the `properties` query parameter as an URL-encoded array of fields to be returned.\nSome default properties are available for all entities: `id`, `name`, `created_at` and `updated_at`.\n",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/resourceIdOptional"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/userIdParam"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/emailParam"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/includeSegmentsParam"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/filteringProperties"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful operation"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/AccessForbidden"
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Param provided is missing or invalid"
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Some other error occurred"
          }
        },
        "summary": "View people",
        "tags": [
          "People"
        ],
        "x-code-samples": [
          {
            "lang": "Curl",
            "source": "curl 'https://api.custify.com/people/5d1eea314ce8477adf5af46c' \\\n -X GET \\\n -H 'Authorization: Bearer <Your access token>' \\\n -H 'Accept: application/json' \\\n -H 'Content-Type: application/json'"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "/playbook": {
      "get": {
        "description": "List playbooks. To list all the playbooks send a `GET` request to [https://api.custify.com/playbook](https://api.custify.com/playbook). To get playbooks for company/people send a `GET` request to [https://api.custify.com/playbook?type=:type](https://api.custify.com/playbook?type=:type). Default type is `companies`.\nTo get a specific playbook send a `GET` request to [https://api.custify.com/playbook/:id](https://api.custify.com/playbook/:id).\n\n### Filtering playbooks\nYou can apply filters using the `filters` query parameter as an URL-encoded array of objects.\n\n### Sorting\nBy default, playbooks are sorted by `position` in ascending order. You can customize sorting using the `sort` and `order` parameters.\n\n### Include counts\nBy default, the response includes company counts (in_progress, completed, etc.). You can disable this by setting `includeCounts=false`.\n",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/itemsPerPageMax200"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/pageParam"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/sortingParam"
          },
          {
            "description": "Type of playbook (companies or people)",
            "in": "query",
            "name": "type",
            "schema": {
              "default": "companies",
              "enum": [
                "companies",
                "people"
              ],
              "example": "companies",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "description": "Filter out scheduled playbooks",
            "in": "query",
            "name": "nonScheduled",
            "schema": {
              "default": false,
              "example": false,
              "type": "boolean"
            }
          },
          {
            "description": "Include company counts in the response",
            "in": "query",
            "name": "includeCounts",
            "schema": {
              "default": true,
              "example": true,
              "type": "boolean"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "properties": {
                    "playbooks": {
                      "description": "An array of objects with the details of the playbooks",
                      "items": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/schemas/PlaybookListing"
                      },
                      "type": "array"
                    },
                    "total": {
                      "description": "Total number of playbooks",
                      "example": 8,
                      "type": "integer"
                    }
                  },
                  "type": "object"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful operation"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/AccessForbidden"
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Some other error occurred"
          }
        },
        "summary": "List playbooks",
        "tags": [
          "Playbooks"
        ],
        "x-code-samples": [
          {
            "lang": "Curl",
            "source": "curl 'https://api.custify.com/playbook?itemsPerPage=20&page=1&type=companies' \\\n -X GET \\\n -H 'Authorization: Bearer <Your access token>' \\\n -H 'Accept: application/json' \\\n -H 'Content-Type: application/json'"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "/segment": {
      "get": {
        "description": "List segments. To list all the segments send a `GET` request to [https://api.custify.com/segment](https://api.custify.com/segment). To get segments for company/people send a `GET` request to [https://api.custify.com/segment?type=:type](https://api.custify.com/segment?type=:type). Default type is `people`.\nTo get a specific segment send a `GET` request to [https://api.custify.com/segment/:id](https://api.custify.com/segment/:id).\n",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/itemsPerPageMax50"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/pageParam"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/sortingParam"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/typeParam"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "properties": {
                    "segments": {
                      "description": "An array of objects with the details of the segments",
                      "items": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/schemas/SegmentsListing"
                      },
                      "type": "array"
                    },
                    "total": {
                      "description": "Total number of segments",
                      "example": 1,
                      "type": "integer"
                    }
                  },
                  "type": "object"
                }
              }
